            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The phrase, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "چڑیا گھر (chiṛyā ghar) is \"bird house\". chiṛyā, \"bird\", comes from Sanskrit caṭaka, \"sparrow\", through a variant ciṭaka (CDIAL 4571). ghar, \"house\", is inherited; it is usually taken as a popular form of Sanskrit gṛha, a link CDIAL calls phonetically difficult (CDIAL 4428)."
            }
          ]
        },
